# Q2. CPU Utilization Problem

## Problem

CPU Utilization = 30%

Scheduler Log:

```text
Ready → Waiting → Ready → Waiting → Ready
```

---

## Root Cause

Processes frequently enter the Waiting state because they spend most of their time waiting for I/O operations.

The CPU remains idle while processes wait.

This is an I/O-bound workload.

---

## Effects

- Low CPU utilization
- Frequent context switching
- Poor system throughput

---

## Optimization

1. Use asynchronous I/O.
2. Increase multiprogramming level.
3. Schedule CPU-bound jobs alongside I/O-bound jobs.
4. Improve disk or device performance.

---

## Conclusion

The CPU is underutilized because processes repeatedly wait for I/O. Better scheduling and asynchronous I/O improve utilization.
